  "description": "Secrets at rest for a self-hosted service: a keyring of 32-byte master keys read from configuration (one current key that seals, older keys that only open until a rekey), each named by an id that opens nothing, and AES-256-GCM sealing with a fresh nonce and associated data that names the row, so a value copied to another row does not open. No master key: the feature that needs it is off and says so; everything else runs.",
